thermonuclear.tooltip.nuclear=Fuel rod block tiers 1-4 allow max parallel: 8/32/128/512\nPower panel parallel setting limits newly loaded fuel batches\nConsumes shortest remaining lifetime first\nDirect generation mode requires a dynamo hatch
thermonuclear.tooltip.breeding=Optional breeding: install paired breeder input/output buses at B positions\nSeparate breeder pool holds up to 512 rods, including pending products\nEvery breeder rod gains whole-reactor pulses x 4 progress per cycle, without division or hull heat bonuses
thermonuclear.tooltip.heat_exchange=Exchanges hot coolant and distilled water for steam, returning cold coolant\nIC2 hot coolant produces only ordinary or superheated steam\nHot super coolant produces only supercritical steam at 5x yield\nHot NaK composite coolant produces only ultra-supercritical steam: 100 L per litre
thermonuclear.tooltip.steam_turbine=No GT rotor required\nEnergy yield: ordinary 1.5 / superheated 4.5 / supercritical 7.5 / ultra-supercritical 10.5 EU/L\nUltra-supercritical steam requires high-pressure shafts; low-pressure shafts support the first three types\nOutput scales with startup progress; returns 1 L distilled water per 160 L steam\nSteam intake limit per cycle can be configured in GUI
